      "title": "START HERE — YuE2 Full Song Instructions",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "<h1>YuE2 Full Song</h1>\n<p><strong>First use only:</strong> Enter a dedicated folder such as <code>E:\\Yue2</code> in <em>target_root</em>, then click <strong>Install Generation + Models</strong> (or <strong>Install Everything</strong> if you also want covers). Installation buttons run only when clicked. Queueing the workflow does not reinstall anything.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Create a song</h2>\n<ol><li>Enter sectioned lyrics in the Generate node using tags such as <code>[Verse]</code>, <code>[Chorus]</code>, <code>[Bridge]</code>, and <code>[Outro]</code>.</li><li>Choose a style preset, type your own comma-separated style description, or use the optional LLM section below.</li><li>Leave <strong>planning_mode = full</strong> for normal songs. Set a seed for repeatable comparisons.</li><li>Queue the workflow. Live stages and token speed appear in the ComfyUI console.</li><li>Preview the result or use the saved copy in <code>ComfyUI/output/audio/YuE2</code>. YuE2 artifacts and metadata are also retained in the reported artifact directory.</li></ol>\n<h2>Optional LLM style helper</h2>\n<p>Edit the short request in <strong>VRGDG_MultiStringConcat</strong>. The LLM converts it into a detailed YuE2 style prompt and sends it to Generate. To bypass the LLM, disconnect the purple style cable and use the preset or editable style box directly. An API key/provider may be required for the selected LLM.</p>\n<h2>Useful settings</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>ode_steps:</strong> controls only final audio synthesis. 32 is the official default; 16 is faster/lower fidelity, while 48–64 is slower with diminishing returns.</li><li><strong>memory_budget_gib:</strong> 30 is reasonable on a 32 GiB GPU; lower it if other applications use VRAM.</li><li><strong>backend:</strong> <code>torch</code> is the fast path; <code>torch-eager</code> is for troubleshooting.</li><li><strong>cfg_scale:</strong> <code>-1</code> uses YuE2 defaults.</li><li><strong>verify_hashes:</strong> leave off for normal runs, especially on slower drives.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Hover over any YuE2 setting for a detailed tooltip.</p>"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "<h1>YuE2 Full Song</h1>\n<p><strong>First use only:</strong> Enter a dedicated folder such as <code>E:\\Yue2</code> in <em>target_root</em>, then click <strong>Install Generation + Models</strong> (or <strong>Install Everything</strong> if you also want covers). Installation buttons run only when clicked. Queueing the workflow does not reinstall anything.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Create a song</h2>\n<ol><li>Enter sectioned lyrics in the Generate node using tags such as <code>[Verse]</code>, <code>[Chorus]</code>, <code>[Bridge]</code>, and <code>[Outro]</code>.</li><li>Choose a style preset, type your own comma-separated style description, or use the optional LLM section below.</li><li>Leave <strong>planning_mode = full</strong> for normal songs. Set a seed for repeatable comparisons.</li><li>Queue the workflow. Live stages and token speed appear in the ComfyUI console.</li><li>Preview the result or use the saved copy in <code>ComfyUI/output/audio/YuE2</code>. YuE2 artifacts and metadata are also retained in the reported artifact directory.</li></ol>\n<h2>Optional LLM style helper</h2>\n<p>Edit the short request in <strong>VRGDG_MultiStringConcat</strong>. The LLM converts it into a detailed YuE2 style prompt and sends it to Generate. To bypass the LLM, disconnect the purple style cable and use the preset or editable style box directly. An API key/provider may be required for the selected LLM.</p>\n<h2>Useful settings</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>ode_steps:</strong> controls only final audio synthesis. 32 is the official default; 16 is faster/lower fidelity, while 48–64 is slower with diminishing returns.</li><li><strong>memory_budget_gib:</strong> 30 is reasonable on a 32 GiB GPU; lower it if other applications use VRAM.</li><li><strong>backend:</strong> <code>torch</code> is the fast path; <code>torch-eager</code> is for troubleshooting.</li><li><strong>cfg_scale:</strong> <code>-1</code> uses YuE2 defaults.</li><li><strong>verify_hashes:</strong> leave off for normal runs, especially on slower drives.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Hover over any YuE2 setting for a detailed tooltip.</p>"
      },
